'''Carrosseries de Balboa, S.A.''' is a Balboan bus and truck bodywork manufacturer based in [[Sant Bart]], with a secondary facility in [[Sant Cristòfor]]. The company designs and builds vehicle bodies on imported chassis, producing transit buses, coaches, and commercial truck bodies for both the domestic market and the [[BTPMEU]] region. It is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker CRR and is a constituent of the [[SCX 100]] index.

The company was founded in 1981 by Sebastià Roca i Biosca, a former maintenance supervisor at the Sant Cristòfor municipal transit authority, who identified that the city's growing bus fleet was being supplied with fully imported vehicles at high cost. Roca established a workshop in Sant Bart to build bus bodies on imported chassis, initially serving the Sant Cristòfor transit network.

Carrosseries de Balboa is the primary domestic supplier of bus bodies for the [[Sant Cristòfor]] public transit network, building bodies on [[BYD Auto|BYD]] electric bus chassis (K8 and K9 models) as well as on chassis from other manufacturers. The company also produces coach bodies for intercity transport operators and truck bodies for commercial logistics companies. The Sant Bart facility handles bus and coach bodywork, while the smaller Sant Cristòfor facility handles truck bodies and specialised vehicle bodies.

Approximately 70 per cent of revenue is derived from domestic contracts, with the remainder from BTPMEU-based transit operators. The company's relationship with BYD — building bodies on BYD electric chassis for the Balboan transit market — is its largest single contract.

